                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e30c7730-02d5-335d-8405-43869a856241",
                        "entry_id": "22b1bd26-8e5c-3761-b1d4-2ba5e1e437c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "церк., высок. одежда из грубой толстой ткани (холста или рогожи), мешковидного полотна, козьего или верблюжьего волоса, надевавшаяся во времена печали, раскаяния, глубокого поста"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c71deb0f-9356-485c-a489-da9bd765760d",
                                "sense_id": "e30c7730-02d5-335d-8405-43869a856241",
                                "text": "Препояшьтесь вретищем и плачьте, священники! рыдайте, служители алтаря! войдите, ночуйте во вретищах, служители Бога моего! ибо не стало в доме Бога вашего хлебного приношения и возлияния."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff503201-93ba-4241-801a-4a8a4d2728d3",
                                "sense_id": "e30c7730-02d5-335d-8405-43869a856241",
                                "text": "Адам с Евой шли по колено в воде вдоль отмели. На них раздувались ветхозаветные вретища."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e35f7f75-ce0f-30ed-be47-aeddb37a400d",
                        "entry_id": "22b1bd26-8e5c-3761-b1d4-2ba5e1e437c6",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., рваная, убогая одежда"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "часто ирон."
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2e004579-c829-41e1-9a70-976648b2af71",
                                "sense_id": "e35f7f75-ce0f-30ed-be47-aeddb37a400d",
                                "text": "Прохожий бедного вида, несчастливец, прикрытый вретищем ― всё это не большая редкость в таком городе, каков Петербург."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6c9badaa-29b0-4bfb-93fe-5bb52c39f9a9",
                                "sense_id": "e35f7f75-ce0f-30ed-be47-aeddb37a400d",
                                "text": "Чиновничишко, накинув на себя какое-то вретище вместо шинели, поплёлся тоже за ним и начал опять ему что-то толковать и внушать."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "575e26cf-e2ea-42c8-ab24-399f15e977e8",
                        "source_entry_id": "22b1bd26-8e5c-3761-b1d4-2ba5e1e437c6",
                        "source_sense_description": "грубая одежда из холста, рогожи, козьего или верблюжьего волоса",
                        "target_lang_word": "sackcloth",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "sackcloth",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ac9bd98-415a-3d2f-b9b9-bd59604c6538",
                                        "entry_id": "1e806646-feb1-384b-a5ce-e4ca0d1a6db8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A coarse hessian style of cloth used to make sacks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e7b39d2b-16af-3068-9caf-8d9ec7f40fb7",
                                        "entry_id": "1e806646-feb1-384b-a5ce-e4ca0d1a6db8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Garments worn as an act of penance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "also",
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "34ced1bc-e0ac-49a6-9a39-51b1c7152828",
                                                "sense_id": "e7b39d2b-16af-3068-9caf-8d9ec7f40fb7",
                                                "text": "After he realised the gravity of his crime he spent some time wearing sackcloth and ashes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37ad63f8-516a-45c8-9077-8e1b44b8422a",
                                                "sense_id": "e7b39d2b-16af-3068-9caf-8d9ec7f40fb7",
                                                "text": "Next you saw her alone, a kneeling penitent at the foot of the crucifix; her long fair hair is unbound, and the sackcloth robe is girded by a cord round her slender shape: her hands are clasped, and tears are flowing fast from the quenched radiance of those shadowy eyes;..."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b79016d0-9649-4ec2-a709-8a12e61d84f0",
                                                "sense_id": "e7b39d2b-16af-3068-9caf-8d9ec7f40fb7",
                                                "text": "No more ashes, no more sackcloth / And an armband made of black cloth / Will someday never more adorn a sleeve"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ab6ac945-2448-41df-9924-3f04feacfd4e",
                        "source_entry_id": "22b1bd26-8e5c-3761-b1d4-2ba5e1e437c6",
                        "source_sense_description": "грубая одежда из холста, рогожи, козьего или верблюжьего волоса",
                        "target_lang_word": "cilice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cilice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cde44876-5ab7-312c-a4cf-806dd4f83a32",
                                        "entry_id": "9d1d7349-fce2-39d7-ac71-f692477db40c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A garment or undergarment made of coarse cloth or animal hair worn close to the skin used by members of various Christian traditions as a self-imposed means of penance (repentance) and mortification of the flesh."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "afd0dd6e-9ca7-4b6d-b478-da13ac30f543",
                                                "sense_id": "cde44876-5ab7-312c-a4cf-806dd4f83a32",
                                                "text": "It was deemed meritorious to disfigure the body by neglect and filth, to extenuate it by fasting and watchfulness, to lacerate it with stripes, and to fret the wounds with cilices of horsehair."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80d2ca38-bd88-33e3-8967-b44c3a26460c",
                                        "entry_id": "9d1d7349-fce2-39d7-ac71-f692477db40c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A leather strap studded with metallic barbs that cut into flesh as a constant reminder of Christ's suffering."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in Opus Dei"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da90da08-016f-486d-a3d6-c795f52f326c",
                                                "sense_id": "80d2ca38-bd88-33e3-8967-b44c3a26460c",
                                                "text": "All she had done was give Teena a cilice, a barbed metal chain she was to tie around her thigh for two hours every day, and a discipline, a rope whip with knotted ends she was to use on her back when she prayed the Hail Mary."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8e0bb016-733b-4863-b96c-db46d8e2bfe0",
                        "source_entry_id": "22b1bd26-8e5c-3761-b1d4-2ba5e1e437c6",
